// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'runtime'. Valid alternatives: ['mapping']
//
// A singleExecEnv is `identifier COLON { serviceMapping (serviceRuntime | serviceRuntimeComponents)+ }`
// -- ORDERED, unlike every other body in this grammar, with `mapping` first and mandatory.
//
// Note what the message says: at this position the only alternative is 'mapping'. That
// ordering is a property of the rule itself rather than of a later validation, and it is the
// opposite of the Service body, where order is free. Getting this backwards produces a
// parser that accepts both orders and refuses neither.
###Service
ExecutionEnvironment fixture::neg::EnvWithoutMapping
{
   executions:
   [
      UAT:
      {
         runtime: fixture::neg::R;
      }
   ];
}
